      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# 1. Dataset Selection\n",
        "\n",
        "I will be using the make_moons function from scikit-learn to generate a dataset to be used for the SVM classifier. The target variable will be class membership (either 0 or 1) because our dataset is binary. It is ideal for SVM while using a kernel because the moons can be separated but not with a straight line."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "-x-c2snU2EvZ"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "7FALbbDqlhIm",
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "outputId": "88fe275e-df68-4821-db34-7060ac21d0e5"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "pandas: 2.2.2\n",
            "numpy: 2.0.2\n",
            "matplotlib: 3.10.0\n",
            "sklearn: 1.6.1\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "import matplotlib\n",
        "import sklearn\n",
        "import random\n",
        "from sklearn.datasets import make_moons\n",
        "\n",
        "seed = 42\n",
        "np.random.seed(seed)\n",
        "random.seed(seed)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Generating the dataset\n",
        "X, y = make_moons(n_samples=350, noise=0.25, random_state=seed)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"pandas: \" + pd.__version__)\n",
        "print(\"numpy: \" + np.__version__)\n",
        "print(\"matplotlib: \" + matplotlib.__version__)\n",
        "print(\"sklearn: \" + sklearn.__version__)\n",
        "\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "#3. Train a Linear SVM"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "Pw936YoL4qnm"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "from sklearn.svm import LinearSVC\n",
        "from sklearn.pipeline import make_pipeline\n",
        "from sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "from sklearn.metrics import accuracy_score, confusion_matrix\n",
        "from sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split\n",
        "\n",
        "# Define test train split\n",
        "X_train, X_test, y_train, y_test = train_test_split(X, y, test_size=0.2, random_state=seed)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Creating the pipeline\n",
        "svm_clf = make_pipeline(StandardScaler(), LinearSVC(random_state=seed, max_iter=10000))\n",
        "\n",
        "# Fitting the model\n",
        "svm_clf.fit(X_train, y_train)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Visualizing the model\n",
        "# Creating the grid\n",
        "x_min, x_max = X_train[:,0].min()-1, X_train[:,0].max()+1\n",
        "y_min, y_max = X_train[:,1].min()-1, X_train[:,1].max()+1\n",
        "\n",
        "xx, yy = np.meshgrid(\n",
        "    np.linspace(x_min, x_max, 300),\n",
        "    np.linspace(y_min, y_max, 300)\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Predict using pipeline (scaling happens automatically)\n",
        "Z = svm_clf.predict(np.c_[xx.ravel(), yy.ravel()])\n",
        "Z = Z.reshape(xx.shape)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Plot decision boundary\n",
        "plt.contourf(xx, yy, Z, alpha=0.3)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Plot TRAIN data only\n",
        "plt.scatter(X_train[:,0], X_train[:,1], c=y_train, edgecolors='k')\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.grid(True, linestyle='--', alpha=0.6)\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.show()\n",
        "\n",
        "# Calculate accuracy score\n",
        "y_pred = svm_clf.predict(X_test)\n",
        "print(\"Accuracy: \", accuracy_score(y_test, y_pred))\n",
        "print(\"Confusion Matrix: \\n\", confusion_matrix(y_test, y_pred))"
      ],
      "metadata": {
