    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Kernels help with non-linear data because data that is not separable in 2 dimensions can often be separated in higher dimensions. The kernels help translate the data into higher dimensions, split the data, and then translate back to 2 dimensions, creating a curved line that better splits the data."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "0iw9aRYxpTek"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "#5. Hyperparameter Tuning"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "q8GfHRO6ptOo"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "from sklearn.model_selection import GridSearchCV\n",
        "\n",
        "# Defining the parameter grid\n",
        "param_grid = {\n",
        "    'svc__C': [0.1, 1, 10, 100, 1000],\n",
        "    'svc__gamma': [0.001, 0.01, 0.1, 1, 10]\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "# Running gridsearch cv\n",
        "grid_search = GridSearchCV(rbf_kernel_svm_clf, param_grid, cv=5, scoring='accuracy')\n",
        "grid_search.fit(X_train, y_train)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Getting results\n",
        "print(\"Best parameters: \", grid_search.best_params_)\n",
        "print(\"Best score: \", grid_search.best_score_)\n"
      ],
